Z||000017||sqoach||02-10-2001||02:05 PM||||ohhhh...ahhhhh...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>i like the rocker panels and the set-back for the wing. very cool.<P>hey twist, what does the kid danger air-damn look like? in fact, what does any of those focoa air-dams and stuff look like? i've been to their site quite a few times, but no pics.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||TwisT||02-10-2001||04:44 PM||||Sqoach,  the FOCOA Kid Danger air-dam is a nice peice.  Sorry,  but I don't have a picture to show...  would be easier to show than to try explaining.<P>The air-dam is not like most others on the market,  where they simply attach to the bottom of the front nose of the GT.  Rather,  it is designed to mount OVER the lower nose and eliminates the "lift" (the section of the nose that protrudes up...  Pontiac designed it that way to avoid curbs and debri).  Doing so gives the GT nose a VERY clean,  level,  and "factory" designed look.    <P>Mine isn't mounted yet (will be this summer along with some other goodies).  I'll try getting a picture made sometime soon.<P>Brett   ||||reg||1
